<header><p class="enc-kicker">Institution</p><h1 class="enc-title">East India Company</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as English East India Company</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The East <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/india">India</a> Company was an English, later British, chartered trading company founded in 1600. Beginning as a trading concern, it became a military and governing power in India, defeating the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/maratha-empire">Maratha Empire</a> and the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sikh-empire">Sikh Empire</a> and reducing the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mughal-empire">Mughal Empire</a> to a pensioner, until the Crown took over in 1858. It was the main instrument of the early <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/british-empire">British Empire</a> in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/asia">Asia</a> and a rival of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/dutch">Dutch</a>, French and other European companies.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/east-india-company.jpg" alt="East India Company" width="320" height="192" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: No machine-readable author provided. Yaddah assumed (based on copyright claims). · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Flag_of_the_British_East_India_Company_(1801).svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
